\description{
The public methods mirror the functional API: \code{is_open()}, \code{fd()},
\code{info()}, \code{set_blocking()}, \code{bind()}, \code{listen()}, \code{accept()}, \code{connect()},
\code{send()}, \code{receive()}, \code{send_to()}, \code{receive_from()}, \code{shutdown()},
\code{close()}, \code{local_name()}, \code{peer_name()}, \code{poll()}, \code{get_option()},
\code{set_option()}, and \code{set_options()}. They delegate to the corresponding
documented functions while retaining the handle as object state.

Use \code{Socket$new_auto()} to create a connected client with IPv4/IPv6
fallback, or \code{Socket$new_listener()} to create a listening server with
IPv4/IPv6 fallback.
